# Exclude patterns for `dux` (see functions.zsh). One basename glob per line;
# both GNU du (--exclude) and BSD du (-I) match with fnmatch against the entry
# name, not the path, so `node_modules` hits it at any depth. Blank lines and
# `#` comments are skipped by the function before the patterns are passed on.
#
# Everything here is regenerable from a lockfile, a compiler, or a cache — the
# stuff that dominates an inode count without telling you anything about what
# you actually wrote. Excluded dirs are pruned, not merely hidden, so they cost
# no stat() calls at all.

